        "kind": "issue",
        "title": "Default git branch should be showing when viewing the repository after it changes",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nOn the pcharbon70/catena repository I tried changing the default branch and now the HEAD and the default branch are out of sync. I changed the git default branch from `rewrite` to `c-otp-asm` and the main page still lands on `rewrite`. The `pun` tool also agrees on the new default branch.\n\n## Running these you can see the reproduction:\n\n`$ git ls-remote --symref https://git.pushin.eu/pcharbon70/catena.git HEAD`\n\n     ref: refs/heads/rewrite\tHEAD\n     8f6fd300d52e0355e1fe46946ff978d78397872b\tHEAD\n\n\n`$ pun repo view -R pcharbon70/catena --json=default_branch,full_name` \n\n {\n  \"default_branch\": \"c-otp-asm\",\n  \"full_name\": \"pcharbon70/catena\"\n}",
        "state": "open",
        "stateRaw": "open",
        "isDraft": false,
        "author": {
